            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "d",
         "prompt": "Let \\( q(x) = \\dfrac{f(x)}{x + 1} \\). Find \\( q'(e) \\). Show the work that leads to your answer.",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "q'(e) = \\frac{2e^{2} + 4e + 1}{e(e + 1)^{2}}",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Quotient rule, with f'(x) from part (a).",
               "latex": "q'(x) = \\frac{\\left( 2\\ln x + \\frac{2x + 1}{x} \\right)(x + 1) - (2x + 1)\\ln x}{(x + 1)^{2}}"
            },
            {
               "text": "At x = e, ln e = 1, so f(e) = 2e + 1 and f'(e) = (4e + 1)/e.",
               "latex": "q'(e) = \\frac{\\frac{4e + 1}{e}(e + 1) - (2e + 1)}{(e + 1)^{2}}"
            },
            {
               "text": "Combine over e.",
               "latex": "q'(e) = \\frac{(4e + 1)(e + 1) - e(2e + 1)}{e(e + 1)^{2}} = \\frac{2e^{2} + 4e + 1}{e(e + 1)^{2}}"
            }
         ],
